/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  nDecane-oXylene -- AN NRTL PAIR FROM EVERY LABORATORY'S MEASUREMENTS.

  WRITTEN BY bin/choupo-curate pair nDecane oXylene (DEV.md 4c C284, the bulk run;
  record docs/design/binary-pairs-from-open-measurements.md section 11).

  THE DECLARATION -- WRITTEN AND COMMITTED BEFORE ANY FIT RAN (several
  declarations of the bulk run share one commit).

  IDENTITY.  nDecane (CAS 124-18-5, InChIKey DIOQZVSQGTUSAI-UHFFFAOYSA-N)
  + oXylene (CAS 95-47-6, InChIKey CTQNGGLPUBDAKN-UHFFFAOYSA-N), joined
  to the archive through identity.json -- never by name.  CLASS (C284): both
  records are volatile molecular liquids (no role nonvolatile/solute, no
  dissociatesTo, no charge, no solid, a vapour-pressure model), and every
  measured temperature lies below both critical temperatures.

  NO MEASURED SERIES IN THIS TREE.  constant/archiveDatasets names each
  dataset (DOI, NIST URL, article sha256, extraction selector, extract
  sha256); `bin/choupo-curate fetch` writes the points into
  constant/archiveExtracts/, which is gitignored.

  STUDIES: every bubble-temperature block of the pair at or below 110 kPa
  with a declared uncertainty (2 block(s)).  FITTED, ALL OF THEM
  (2):
      10.1016/j.fluid.2012.09.019    block 12   11 pts  20 kPa  366.11-391.33 K  U 0.12-0.14 K
      10.1016/j.fluid.2004.10.027    block 24    5 pts  95.8 kPa  417.45-434.95 K  U 1.01-1.01 K
        (reports x of the other member: written as x[nDecane] = 1 - x by --x-of)
  SET ASIDE BY THE EXTRACTION RULES, BY NAME:
      (none)

  THE RULE (DEV.md 4c C283 amended, C284).  Every laboratory above is
  fitted; none is held out (the C16 partition and its band are retired as
  the acceptance test).  NRTL, a_ij = a_ji = 0, alpha = 0.30 fixed: two
  parameters (b_ij, b_ji); each point weighted by 1/U, U its own stated
  expanded uncertainty.  Objective twoStage (least squares, then minimax;
  T_bubble absolute, in K).  OUTLIERS: after a least-squares stage over every
  point, a point with |T_model - T| > 3 K is discarded BY
  NAME (`discard` on its evidence entry, listed below) and the fit repeated
  without it.
  THE GRADED ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C285, applied to pairs by C286): max
  |T_model - T| over the KEPT points is GRADED -- clean up to 1 K,
  warning up to 2 K, severe up to 4 K, refused above; a point with no
  bubble point refuses. C283's relative clause (5 / 10 / 20 %) judges
  composition; this fit has no composition residual, so only the
  temperature clause applies. Every grade but refused is accepted and
  promoted (autoPromoted, humanReviewed false) with `fitGrade` and its
  max |dT| in the record's provenance; the engine voices a warning or a
  severe grade on every run that reads the pair. A pair that splits ONE
  liquid inside its validity span is not promoted, whatever its grade
  (arm f).
  Two starts: (0, 0) and (800, -400).

  OUTLIERS DISCARDED AFTER THE LEAST-SQUARES STAGE:
  @@OUTLIERS-BEGIN@@
      1 point(s) of 16: doi 10.1016/j.fluid.2004.10.027 row 2: x 0.7124,
      P 95.800 kPa, T 430.95 K, dT +3.11 K
  @@OUTLIERS-END@@

  @@MODELS-BEGIN@@
  THE OTHER ACTIVITY MODELS (DEV.md 4c C294), declared before their fits
  ran. The SAME datasets and the SAME kept points as fit_nrtl: each op
  below is fit_nrtl copied verbatim -- evidence, discards, objective,
  residual, weighting, options -- with only its parameters, its `thermo
  {}` fragment (the model) and its outputs changed; the outlier discard
  was decided ONCE, on the NRTL least-squares stage, and is reused, never
  re-decided per model. UNIQUAC: two parameters a_ij, a_ji (K), tau_ij =
  exp(-a_ij/T), b = c = 0 fixed (the NRTL default's count; temperature
  dependence 1/T), r and q each component's own record. Wilson: two
  parameters A_ij, A_ji (J/mol), Lambda_ij = (V_j/V_i) exp(-A_ij/RT), V
  the records' Vliq. Two starts each. Each model gets its own record
  (constant/parameters/<MODEL>/), its own grade at 1 / 2 / 4 K (max
  |T_model - T|), its own one-liquid test (arm f), `fitGradeBasis
  inSample`, the C300 cap and `review { by none; }`; a severe or refused
  grade, or a split, is not promoted. The three in-sample residuals are
  published side by side, never used to choose a model for the student.
  UNIQUAC: FITTED. Wilson: FITTED.
  @@MODELS-END@@

  @@MODELS-RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE UNIQUAC AND WILSON FITS FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured,
  not argued). Beside fit_nrtl's max |dT| 2.699 K (severe) on the same
  kept points. fit_uniquac: a_ij = -210.6, a_ji = 298.5 K over 15 kept
  points: max |dT| 2.456 K, mean 0.381 K, graded severe -> accepted;
  fit_uniquac_start2 lands on A DIFFERENT pair (211.9, -165.0). PROMOTED
  on 2026-11-12 into
  data/standards/parameters/UNIQUAC/nDecane-oXylene.dat as reviewStatus
  autoPromoted, review by none, because: fit grade severe -- max |dT|
  2.456 K over the 15 kept points, one liquid across the validity span;
  BEATS THE IDEAL MIXTURE (C334): 2.4555 K against ideal 3.1657 K.
  fit_wilson: A_ij = -3472.2, A_ji = 4449.6 J/mol over 15 kept points:
  max |dT| 2.258 K, mean 0.431 K, graded severe -> accepted;
  fit_wilson_start2 lands on the same pair (-3472.2, 4449.6). PROMOTED on
  2026-11-12 into data/standards/parameters/Wilson/nDecane-oXylene.dat as
  reviewStatus autoPromoted, review by none, because: fit grade severe --
  max |dT| 2.258 K over the 15 kept points, one liquid across the
  validity span; BEATS THE IDEAL MIXTURE (C334): 2.2584 K against ideal
  3.1657 K.
  @@MODELS-RESULT-END@@

  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  fit_nrtl: b_ij = -293.0 K, b_ji = 408.0 K over 15 kept points of 2
  laboratories (1 discarded): max |dT| 2.699 K, mean 0.416 K, graded
  severe (limits 1 / 2 / 4 K) -> accepted. fit_nrtl_start2 lands on the
  same pair (-293.0, 408.0). PROMOTED on 2026-11-10 into
  data/standards/parameters/NRTL/nDecane-oXylene.dat as reviewStatus
  autoPromoted, humanReviewed false, because: fit grade severe -- max
  |dT| 2.699 K over the 15 kept points (limits 1 / 2 / 4 K), one liquid
  across the validity span
  @@RESULT-END@@

  EARLIER FITS, SUPERSEDED BY THIS DECLARATION
  @@EARLIER-BEGIN@@
  C283 amended + C284, the bulk run of 2026-11-10: every laboratory
  fitted, outliers beyond 3 K discarded by name, accepted only below 1 K
  (superseded by the graded acceptance of C285, applied to pairs by C286;
  this declaration keeps the same studies, the same outlier rule and the
  same discards -- nothing re-partitioned): WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in
  `expected`; measured, not argued). fit_nrtl: b_ij = -293.0 K, b_ji =
  408.0 K over 15 kept points of 2 laboratories (1 discarded): max |dT|
  2.699 K, mean 0.416 K against the acceptance 1 K -> notAccepted.
  fit_nrtl_start2 lands on the same pair (-293.0, 408.0). NOT PROMOTABLE:
  max |dT| 2.699 K over the 15 kept points is not below 1 K
  @@EARLIER-END@@

  WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED.  The pair is correct at these pressures and in this
  frame (ideal-gas vapour, the catalogue's own vapour-pressure records); the
  measurements were transcribed by the archive and have NOT been read back
  against the articles (the CHECKLIST that `fetch` writes is the aid).
